{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund specialist NHS wards for people with learning disabilities and autism",
        "additional_details": "People with learning disabilities and autism can experience unnecessary distress when receiving hospital care. Overwhelming environments, poor understanding of complex needs and inadequate facilities can turn a hospital visit into a terrifying experience. Families should never have to fight for basic dignity, safety and compassion. Every patient deserves appropriate care, regardless of their disability. This needs to change.",
        "background": "We want the Government to fund specialist wards in major NHS hospitals and smaller safe haven units in other hospitals for children & adults with learning disabilities, autism and complex needs. These should offer sensory-friendly spaces, accessible facilities, specialist equipment and trained staff",
